# Provability

## N0 proof surface

N0 proves the repository-control capability, not an invented product domain.
`proof/policy.toml` supplies the shared discovery configuration and
`proof/repoctl/` declares the active laws. The generated package
`{{ package }}._foundation` is an empty behavior boundary until a real
capability exists.

Each declared law names its production target, scope, assumptions, independent
oracle, `icontract` condition, Hypothesis evidence, and CrossHair target. The
proof guard rejects a missing link before the evidence suite runs.

## Evidence sequence

1. Run `just prove` after changing a repository-control law or its evidence.
2. Run `just proof-report` to inspect the active property/evidence matrix.
3. Run `just prove-deep` only when a larger generated, stateful, or symbolic
   search is warranted.
4. Run `just check` before handoff; coverage is a floor, not proof.

The shipped properties cover capability planning, derived-index exactness,
ownership-path closure, application replay, activation, and retirement. Their
canonical evidence lives under `verification/repoctl/` and
`verification/tests/test_repoctl_evidence.py`.

## Independent oracles

An oracle accepts explicit facts and returns `bool`. It must not import or call
the behavior it judges, read ambient state, perform I/O, or recover a result by
re-running production code. Keep the oracle beside the repository-control
decision it describes, such as
`repoctl/modules/repository_generation/domain/specifications.py`.

## Canaries and symbolic evidence

Every law has a plausible falsifying canary. The symbolic layer also runs
`verification/harness/symbolic_canary.py`, whose deliberately false
`refutable_echo` postcondition must be refuted. A symbolic run that finds no
target is not accepted as evidence.

## Future capability laws

Do not create a product property before a product capability exists. When one
is declared, add its catalog, oracle, production contract, Hypothesis evidence,
and symbolic target as one coherent vertical change. The same proof guard will
then aggregate it with repository-control evidence.
